WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.034 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-You were not always --

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
At a young age,
people probably assumed

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you were talking about
international news

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
from behind a desk,
but you --

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Your first on-camera job

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:11.444
was you were in an adaptation of
Charles Dickens' "Bleak House."

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.313 line:92%
-So, that is actually true.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-You know what? That's true.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
We do have to hammer home
that that's true,

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause that sounds like a joke
you would make.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:21.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It also sounds
like an offensive stereotype

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:22.555 size:84% position:42% line:92%
about a British person.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You were all probably in
Dickensian dramas growing up."

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sadly, I was.
So, yeah.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.630
No one has really found this out
here other than your staff.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here's a photo.
-This is it.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.667 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is what the President
has done to me.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:37.904 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:41.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, there's a child
with light in his eyes there.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:44.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, so...

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
Basically,
when I was 6 years old,

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
the BBC was shooting
a costume drama

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
called "Bleak House"
nearby my school,

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:55.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they wanted a kid
with dark hair and brown eyes,

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.856 line:92%
and I was two for two on that.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:01:01.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, I was in this, like,
very, very lavish

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:05.632
Dickensian drama for the BBC
with, like, Dame Diana Rigg.

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't understand
what anything was.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't know
what was happening.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:11.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
They just said,
"Do you want to do this?"

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Is it
at the same time as school?"

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said, "Yes,
you'll have to leave school,"

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:18.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said yes before
they ended that conversation.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, it was
a very, very weird experience.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.281 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Here's a clip.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.615
I believe your character's name
is Felix.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
I was Felix Pardiggle,

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm an orphan.
-Okay.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:27.587 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:31.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You may have seen the names
of my five boys

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:33.927 line:92%
printed on a subscription list.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:38.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
Felix, eight pence,
to the Superannuated Widows.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Wow, really good.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:43.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
Really good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
Thank you.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:48.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is like one more element
of the stereotype,

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that you played an orphan.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.245 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-It is so offensive.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
If I'd spent half my childhood
up a chimney,

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's the only way
that you could make that

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
more reductive view
of British people.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
The amazing thing
about that scene,

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.921
the only thing I remember
about it is them saying,

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, you need
to act bored now."

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember thinking,
"Oh, that's okay.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am bored."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.864
-My parents watched a ton of PBS
when we were growing up.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:12.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
They watched
a ton of costume dramas.

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every one of them,
from my perspective,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
could've been called
"Bleak House."

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:18.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is absolutely fair.
That's right.

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:21.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's an
all-encompassing title.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:22.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
Actually, the only other thing
I remember from that

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:25.011
was Diana Rigg,
who was, like, one of the great

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:28.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
British actresses, she gave me
aniseed balls on set.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know --
What are aniseed balls?

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You don't have
aniseed balls here?

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.920
-No.
-Right, 'cause you value flavor.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:34.787 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is anyone here from Britain?
-Yes.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah,
do you remember aniseed balls?

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:39.492 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I do, indeed.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, were they pleasant
to put in your face?

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.996 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-No, they're disgusting.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.398 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:47.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. They are --
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:51.971 line:92%
-They are absolutely disgusting.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then what --
And when you --

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.375 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.809 line:92%
By the way that's the most --

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:59.245 size:84% position:42%
I've never seen someone
so effectively interact

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
with an audience member
on our show.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:01.814 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you were so clear --
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is the way
that British people

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.253 line:92%
reminisce about their past.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.756 size:84% position:42%
"Do you remember that?"
"Yes, it was awful."

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:11.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Me too."
-Yeah.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:12.592 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

